/target/
/sensor/target/
/hermes/target/
/companion-gateway/target/
/tests/harness/target/
/consent-cache/target/
/collector/target/
.env
# Backups a deploy edit leaves beside it: the same secrets, never versioned
.env.bak*
# Secret files an operator keeps at the root under their own names — the OpenRAG
# token (`token-or.env`, `token_OpenRAG.env`) and the like. `.env` alone did not
# cover these: `token-or.env` holds a live `or-<32 hex>` bearer and was one
# `git add -A` from being committed. A `*.env` name at the root is a secret file
# by convention here, whatever it is called.
/*.env
# A dump of the host's Docker state (containers, images, env). It prints every
# container's environment, so it is the same class of secret as a `.env`.
.docker-snapshot-*.txt

# Python bytecode, from running the SDK's own unit tests
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent tooling: local skills installs and agent worktrees, never versioned
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json

# Playwright MCP session artefacts
.playwright-mcp/
